(5168493, 746705, 97166, '<td valign="top">When he was brought before her, the confusion was clear on his face.  He had been arrested by these people, accused of being a spy, a charge punishable by death.  So when he was led here, to be faced only by this woman, shamelessly disrobed, it was all he could do not to let out a surprised laugh. This was to be his judge?  <br/> <br/>So when she suddenly grinned ominously, and raised her fingers to her temples, he did begin to laugh, but that laugh was choked off suddenly as his eyes met hers, and became utterly and completely lost within them. <br/> <br/>He felt dizzy, sick, and in some deep part of his mind suddenly realized what was happening.  She was probing his mind.  Digging into his thoughts and secrets.  Before he could even begin to resist she mined everything he had ever known, everything he ever was, and tore it from him unceremoniously.<br/> <br/>As blood suddenly began to run from his ears, his nose, his eyes, and he convulsed a few final times in the arms of his captives before finally becoming forever still, the woman suddenly blinked and cut her contact.<br/> <br/>"Innocent."  They were her only words. She cast a disgusted glance at the men that had brought him in and then faded back through a curtain that lay behind her.</td>', 'When he was brought before her, the confusion was clear on his face.  He had been arrested by these people, accused of being a spy, a charge punishable by death.  So when he was led here, to be faced only by this woman, shamelessly disrobed, it was all he could do not to let out a surprised laugh. This was to be his judge?   So when she suddenly grinned ominously, and raised her fingers to her temples, he did begin to laugh, but that laugh was choked off suddenly as his eyes met hers, and became utterly and completely lost within them.  He felt dizzy, sick, and in some deep part of his mind suddenly realized what was happening.  She was probing his mind.  Digging into his thoughts and secrets.  Before he could even begin to resist she mined everything he had ever known, everything he ever was, and tore it from him unceremoniously. As blood suddenly began to run from his ears, his nose, his eyes, and he convulsed a few final times in the arms of his captives before finally becoming forever still, the woman suddenly blinked and cut her contact. "Innocent."  They were her only words. She cast a disgusted glance at the men that had brought him in and then faded back through a curtain that lay behind her.', '2009-01-03 20:11:58.000000', NULL, 1),
