(5175214, 746175, 97166, '<td valign="top">It descended from the heavens, to settle between the trees.  There it sat, and slowly spun, the message upon it terrestrial, but this was no terrestrial object.<br/> <br/>From whence did it come?  Why was it here?  What purpose could it possibly have to visit this planet yet tell us of things we already knew?  The human DNA helix, the continents, earthly language.  <br/> <br/>What did it all mean?  So they gathered, the people of earth. They gathered and tried to figure it out. They gathered in awe and confusion and curiosity.<br/> <br/>They gathered, and then, they died.<br/> <br/>When it was all over, it began to spin once more, and lifted above the trees and vanished into the heavens.</td>', 'It descended from the heavens, to settle between the trees.  There it sat, and slowly spun, the message upon it terrestrial, but this was no terrestrial object. From whence did it come?  Why was it here?  What purpose could it possibly have to visit this planet yet tell us of things we already knew?  The human DNA helix, the continents, earthly language.   What did it all mean?  So they gathered, the people of earth. They gathered and tried to figure it out. They gathered in awe and confusion and curiosity. They gathered, and then, they died. When it was all over, it began to spin once more, and lifted above the trees and vanished into the heavens.', '2009-01-06 16:32:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5175231, 749729, 92010, '<td valign="top">ha. what a scraggly beard.  just how i pictured santa.</td>', 'ha. what a scraggly beard.  just how i pictured santa.', '2009-01-06 16:47:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5175236, 750162, 97166, '<td valign="top">The wind whisked her hair as she stood there, looking out over the world, so many miles from home. A single tear built in the corner of her eye, and her mind ran through so many things. They whys, the why nots, the hows, the how nots, the what could bes, the what shouldn''t bes.   Her companion slowly walked over and nudged her shoulder, perhaps because of some emphathy they shared.  She smiled sadly and scratched his nose, and lay her head against him.  <br/> <br/>It was a hard world sometimes, and she just had to get away, to come out here where her father and her had come so many times before.  To this place where they would talk and laugh and he would teach her so very much about the land and the trees and birds and the way things worked.  Now, she was here alone, and he would never come with her again.  <br/> <br/>The tears flowed more freely now, and the wind continued to blow, and upon it it seemed to whisper to her in his voice, to let her know that eventually it would be all right.  Eventually.  <br/> <br/>With one last tear-filled gaze at their special place, she got back on the horse that had been her father''s favorite, now passed to her, and hugged him tight, and together they began the journey home.</td>', 'The wind whisked her hair as she stood there, looking out over the world, so many miles from home. A single tear built in the corner of her eye, and her mind ran through so many things. They whys, the why nots, the hows, the how nots, the what could bes, the what shouldn''t bes.   Her companion slowly walked over and nudged her shoulder, perhaps because of some emphathy they shared.  She smiled sadly and scratched his nose, and lay her head against him.   It was a hard world sometimes, and she just had to get away, to come out here where her father and her had come so many times before.  To this place where they would talk and laugh and he would teach her so very much about the land and the trees and birds and the way things worked.  Now, she was here alone, and he would never come with her again.   The tears flowed more freely now, and the wind continued to blow, and upon it it seemed to whisper to her in his voice, to let her know that eventually it would be all right.  Eventually.   With one last tear-filled gaze at their special place, she got back on the horse that had been her father''s favorite, now passed to her, and hugged him tight, and together they began the journey home.', '2009-01-06 16:54:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5175239, 750200, 97166, '<td valign="top">She did not know what this stuff was, but oh, the fun! <br/> <br/>She ran and jumped and rolled and dug and flung about.  She nipped and barked and chased.  <br/> <br/>She did not know what this stuff was, but she was glad to have discovered it, and hoped that it would never go away, and even has it clung to her and got in her eyes and started to soak her to the skin, she wouldn''t have it any other way.</td>', 'She did not know what this stuff was, but oh, the fun!  She ran and jumped and rolled and dug and flung about.  She nipped and barked and chased.   She did not know what this stuff was, but she was glad to have discovered it, and hoped that it would never go away, and even has it clung to her and got in her eyes and started to soak her to the skin, she wouldn''t have it any other way.', '2009-01-06 16:56:36.000000', NULL, 1),
