(5181935, 751170, 48954, '<td valign="top">great crisp colors!</td>', 'great crisp colors!', '2009-01-09 09:14:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5181956, 749684, 14867, '<td valign="top">The strange thing is that the yellow ribbon of the FS-challenge (the superb <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=749900" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/960/120/749900.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/960/120/749900.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/960/120/749900.jpg"/></a>) is actually showing a suffering animal.</td>', 'The strange thing is that the yellow ribbon of the FS-challenge (the superb ) is actually showing a suffering animal.', '2009-01-09 09:51:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5182026, 751428, 73564, '<td valign="top">Nice image and colors, seems a bit oof, are you using a tripod? Using a slower shutter would have made it flow nicely, maybe bringing the iso down to 100, that would help with the brightness....not sure about the frame, its too thick...but don''t know until you try it, nicely done...good job...</td>', 'Nice image and colors, seems a bit oof, are you using a tripod? Using a slower shutter would have made it flow nicely, maybe bringing the iso down to 100, that would help with the brightness....not sure about the frame, its too thick...but don''t know until you try it, nicely done...good job...', '2009-01-09 11:06:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5182089, 751170, 44825, '<td valign="top">Fabulous!<br/> <br/>There is no such thing as a perfect shot but if there were this would be it!<br/> <br/>I love the sky and Mt Ranier in the background and the lighting and the composition. Brilliant<br/> <br/>A well deserved ribbon.</td>', 'Fabulous! There is no such thing as a perfect shot but if there were this would be it! I love the sky and Mt Ranier in the background and the lighting and the composition. Brilliant A well deserved ribbon.', '2009-01-09 12:12:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5182109, 751170, 4793, '<td valign="top">Beautiful photo of this wonderful city</td>', 'Beautiful photo of this wonderful city', '2009-01-09 12:22:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5182131, 749684, 18197, '<td valign="top">I dont like the subject, but the quality of your photo is superb. It''s clear that at least you''re using your photo talent to communicate something you think is important. I have a lot of respect for a photographer who is willing to push out of the usual-DPC-Stock box and show us something new and (sometimes) risky. However unpleasant folks found the subject, it was an incredible photo to convey such a strong emotional payload.<br/> <br/>In my view the final average score reflects folks'' queasiness about the subject, not the quality of the photo.<br/> <br/>One of the values of any art form is to make people think. And some of the world''s great art is explicitly designed to make people think about hard things, unpleasant things, things that are wrong ... sometimes just to expose them, sometimes to initiate change. <br/> <br/>Many of the photos at DPC are as empty of meaning as sugar is empty of nutrition. Sometimes we need a little protein in our diets. And it''s refreshing to see a photo that makes us think. In the same way there''s nothing wrong with an occasional lollipop, there''s nothing wrong with the occasional cute puppy, the tiger''s head, the waterdrop, the illuminated glassware, the motion-blurred seashore at sunset and so on. But there''s also nothing wrong with the occasional photo that makes us think, react, feel.<br/> <br/>Thanks for taking the risk.</td>', 'I dont like the subject, but the quality of your photo is superb. It''s clear that at least you''re using your photo talent to communicate something you think is important. I have a lot of respect for a photographer who is willing to push out of the usual-DPC-Stock box and show us something new and (sometimes) risky. However unpleasant folks found the subject, it was an incredible photo to convey such a strong emotional payload. In my view the final average score reflects folks'' queasiness about the subject, not the quality of the photo. One of the values of any art form is to make people think. And some of the world''s great art is explicitly designed to make people think about hard things, unpleasant things, things that are wrong ... sometimes just to expose them, sometimes to initiate change.  Many of the photos at DPC are as empty of meaning as sugar is empty of nutrition. Sometimes we need a little protein in our diets. And it''s refreshing to see a photo that makes us think. In the same way there''s nothing wrong with an occasional lollipop, there''s nothing wrong with the occasional cute puppy, the tiger''s head, the waterdrop, the illuminated glassware, the motion-blurred seashore at sunset and so on. But there''s also nothing wrong with the occasional photo that makes us think, react, feel. Thanks for taking the risk.', '2009-01-09 12:55:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5182132, 749684, 26464, '<td valign="top">this kind of thing would work well in ma gallery where people will likely appreciate it, not on a site where people vote with their gut mostly. <br/></td>', 'this kind of thing would work well in ma gallery where people will likely appreciate it, not on a site where people vote with their gut mostly. ', '2009-01-09 12:56:52.000000', NULL, 0),
