(5365996, 750809, 30982, '<td valign="top">This one scored well, especially as a flower in a free study.  What it has going for it - good rich vibrant color, good simple (but not too simple) composition, very good detail and effective use of DOF.  There''s very little noise - Canons are good at that at higher ISOs - but in looking at your settings you could have easily cranked the ISO down a few and still had a good shutter speed.  (Then again, if you''re like me, you have it set for something and forget to change it.  I do that all the time.)</td>', 'This one scored well, especially as a flower in a free study.  What it has going for it - good rich vibrant color, good simple (but not too simple) composition, very good detail and effective use of DOF.  There''s very little noise - Canons are good at that at higher ISOs - but in looking at your settings you could have easily cranked the ISO down a few and still had a good shutter speed.  (Then again, if you''re like me, you have it set for something and forget to change it.  I do that all the time.)', '2009-03-15 17:20:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5366227, 750809, 12250, '<td valign="top">Actually the shutter speed was more of a what if scenario.  There were a bunch of bees flying in an out pretty quickly so I figured that I may get lucky with on of the snaps.  I did catch a couple of bees but they were OOF.<br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> This one scored well, especially as a flower in a free study.  What it has going for it - good rich vibrant color, good simple (but not too simple) composition, very good detail and effective use of DOF.  There''s very little noise - Canons are good at that at higher ISOs - but in looking at your settings you could have easily cranked the ISO down a few and still had a good shutter speed.  (Then again, if you''re like me, you have it set for something and forget to change it.  I do that all the time.) </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Actually the shutter speed was more of a what if scenario.  There were a bunch of bees flying in an out pretty quickly so I figured that I may get lucky with on of the snaps.  I did catch a couple of bees but they were OOF.Originally posted by Melethia: This one scored well, especially as a flower in a free study.  What it has going for it - good rich vibrant color, good simple (but not too simple) composition, very good detail and effective use of DOF.  There''s very little noise - Canons are good at that at higher ISOs - but in looking at your settings you could have easily cranked the ISO down a few and still had a good shutter speed.  (Then again, if you''re like me, you have it set for something and forget to change it.  I do that all the time.) ', '2009-03-15 17:45:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5378001, 751290, 24454, '<td valign="top">I love it too, Ancur.   You captured more than a beautiful sunset.  You captured such a beautiful moment in time.  I feel such a wonderful memory when I look at this photo, and I think someday, when your daughter is all grown up, it will be more precious to you and your wife than you can ever imagine.   I love getting to share this moment with you thru your photography!</td>', 'I love it too, Ancur.   You captured more than a beautiful sunset.  You captured such a beautiful moment in time.  I feel such a wonderful memory when I look at this photo, and I think someday, when your daughter is all grown up, it will be more precious to you and your wife than you can ever imagine.   I love getting to share this moment with you thru your photography!', '2009-03-16 21:56:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5379482, 751290, 58715, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SandyP:</b></div><hr/><i> I love it too, Ancur.   You captured more than a beautiful sunset.  You captured such a beautiful moment in time.  I feel such a wonderful memory when I look at this photo, and I think someday, when your daughter is all grown up, it will be more precious to you and your wife than you can ever imagine.   I love getting to share this moment with you thru your photography! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Sandy,<br/> <br/>Thanks a lot for your comments. Certainly This photo is one of my photos that I love the most. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by SandyP: I love it too, Ancur.   You captured more than a beautiful sunset.  You captured such a beautiful moment in time.  I feel such a wonderful memory when I look at this photo, and I think someday, when your daughter is all grown up, it will be more precious to you and your wife than you can ever imagine.   I love getting to share this moment with you thru your photography!   Hi Sandy, Thanks a lot for your comments. Certainly This photo is one of my photos that I love the most.  ', '2009-03-17 01:00:07.000000', NULL, 0),
