(5417008, 751439, 66515, '<td valign="top">What an excellent capture. It appears that you used HDR and quite effectively too. (I hate when it results in a really overprocessed look). <br/> <br/>Great shot.</td>', 'What an excellent capture. It appears that you used HDR and quite effectively too. (I hate when it results in a really overprocessed look).  Great shot.', '2009-04-03 14:13:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5417059, 751160, 74559, '<td valign="top">Well, as an astronomer and avid sky watcher, I certainly appreciate this image! We get a lot of these in New Mexico too. This is indeed a beautiful solar halo, and I know what you mean about not being able to fit the whole thing in the image; it wasn''t until I got a wide angle lens that I could manage it :-) BTW, this is a solar halo, not a sundog; sundogs are little colored spots of refracted light that occur in specific orientations, often ocurring along with a solar halo, but often without a solar halo. Whatever, this is a lovely image!</td>', 'Well, as an astronomer and avid sky watcher, I certainly appreciate this image! We get a lot of these in New Mexico too. This is indeed a beautiful solar halo, and I know what you mean about not being able to fit the whole thing in the image; it wasn''t until I got a wide angle lens that I could manage it :-) BTW, this is a solar halo, not a sundog; sundogs are little colored spots of refracted light that occur in specific orientations, often ocurring along with a solar halo, but often without a solar halo. Whatever, this is a lovely image!', '2009-04-03 14:52:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5443452, 750230, 88136, '<td valign="top">took me forever to hunt this down, i couldn''t remember how long ago it had been taken. anyways, a new fav for slippy:)</td>', 'took me forever to hunt this down, i couldn''t remember how long ago it had been taken. anyways, a new fav for slippy:)', '2009-04-19 02:25:07.000000', NULL, 0),
